# The permanent raw snapshot of what each state agency served us (N6b). Gitignored because it is
# hundreds of MB of third-party data, but — unlike `.scratch/` — it is **not** disposable: it is the
# archive that makes reprocessing free and survives a state reorganising its portal. Mirror it with
# `mirror-r2.sh push` rather than deleting it. See README §"The two caches".
.raw/

# Derived intermediates only: reprojected GeoJSON, interpolation grids, gdal_contour output, the
# .pmtiles. Safe to `rm -rf` at any moment — everything here rebuilds from `.raw/` with no network.
.scratch/

# rclone remote + bucket for the raw mirror. Holds no secrets (those live in ~/.config/rclone).
.env.local

# GMT writes its "common arguments shelf" into the working directory on every invocation, so this is
# per-run scratch that would otherwise churn the diff with the last lake's bounding box.
gmt.history
